    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sqrt{7}\\approx2.65$, $2.7=2.70$, $\\sqrt[3]{18}\\approx2.62$, $2\\pi\\approx6.28$, $\\sqrt{2}\\approx1.41$.\n\nLeft to right: $\\sqrt{2},\\ \\sqrt[3]{18},\\ \\sqrt{7},\\ 2.7,\\ 2\\pi$.",
      "worked": "Calculate each approximation to 2 decimal places:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{7}&\\approx2.65\\\\2.7&=2.70\\\\\\sqrt[3]{18}&\\approx2.62\\\\2\\pi&\\approx6.28\\\\\\sqrt{2}&\\approx1.41\\end{align*}$$\nMark these positions on one number line. Between $2$ and $3$, $\\sqrt[3]{18}$ is just left of $\\sqrt{7}$, and both are left of $2.7$.",
